course: dictionary
lesson: 3071
title: Edelweiss, a mountain flower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing you could picture, and edelweiss is one of them. The dictionary says it is a small white flower that grows high in the Alps and other mountains of Europe. Read this sentence: «Edelweiss is covered in thick woolly white hairs that protect it from strong sunlight, cold and drying wind.» The clues woolly and white tell you what it looks like, and high mountains tell you where it lives.
explain: The context also explains why the flower looks the way it does. The hairs work like a coat, keeping the plant warm and stopping it from drying out in cold, windy places. Woolly means soft and fluffy, like wool.
explain: Edelweiss is also a special symbol. It stands for Switzerland and Austria, and it is the name of a famous song from the film «The Sound of Music». When you meet a word in a song or on a country's badge, check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Edelweiss is a small white flower that grows high in the Alps and other mountains of Europe.
fact: «Woolly» means soft and fluffy, like wool.
fact: The thick white hairs on edelweiss protect it from strong sunlight, cold and drying wind.
fact: Edelweiss is a famous symbol of Switzerland and Austria.
fact: Edelweiss is protected in many places, so you must not pick it there.
exercise: «Edelweiss is covered in thick woolly white hairs.» What does woolly mean here? | Hot to touch | Wet and slippery | Hard and sharp like a rock | *Soft and fluffy, like wool
exercise: Where does edelweiss grow? | In hot deserts | Deep under the ground | Low in the fields by the sea | *High in the Alps and other mountains of Europe
exercise: «Edelweiss is protected, so it must not be picked in many places.» What does protected mean here? | *Kept safe by rules | Picked for dinner | Growing in every garden | Very tall and thin
test: What is edelweiss a symbol of? | Norway and Sweden | Spain and Portugal | Italy and France | *Switzerland and Austria
test: Which famous song takes its name from edelweiss? | The Lion King | Frozen | Mary Poppins | *The Sound of Music
exam: Why must you not pick edelweiss in many places? | It is too small to see | *Because it is protected by rules there | It is poisonous to touch | It only grows in summer
